    "post_content": "Day 3 of 30: Practical SQL & Business Analytics Challenges\nTopic: Conditional Aggregation: Advertisement Tap-Through Rate (Beginner)\n\nA fintech app needed to measure ad effectiveness without running multiple queries or expensive subqueries. Here is how conditional aggregation solves it.\n\nThe Business Scenario:\nTable ad_events contains raw interaction events:\n(event_id, ad_id, event_type, user_id, event_time)\nWhere event_type can be 'impression', 'tap', or 'dismiss'.\n\nYou need to compute the Tap-Through Rate (TTR) per ad_id as: (total taps / total impressions) * 100.0, rounded to 2 decimal places.\n\nThe Challenge:\nWhich query correctly and cleanly computes the TTR in a single scan?\n\nA) SELECT ad_id, ROUND(100.0 * COUNT(CASE WHEN event_type = 'tap' THEN 1 END) / NULLIF(COUNT(CASE WHEN event_type = 'impression' THEN 1 END), 0), 2) AS tap_rate FROM ad_events GROUP BY ad_id;\nB) SELECT ad_id, ROUND(100.0 * SUM(event_type = 'tap') / SUM(event_type = 'impression'), 2) AS tap_rate FROM ad_events WHERE event_type IN ('tap', 'impression');\nC) SELECT ad_id, COUNT('tap') / COUNT('impression') * 100 FROM ad_events GROUP BY ad_id;\nD) SELECT ad_id, AVG(event_type) * 100 FROM ad_events GROUP BY ad_id;\n\nDrop your answer (A, B, C, or D) in the comments along with your reasoning.\nTomorrow at 01:30 PM IST, we post the complete engineering breakdown and SQL solution in the comments.\n\nNIKHILs TECH Studio | India's Practice Gym for the AI Era\nLearn. Practice. Simulate. Grow.\n\n#SQL #DataAnalytics #DataEngineering #BusinessIntelligence #InterviewPrep #TechCareers #NTSCommand",
    "answer_comment": "Day 3 Solution Breakdown: Conditional Aggregation: Advertisement Tap-Through Rate\nCorrect Answer: Option A\n\nWhy this is the correct engineering approach:\nThe SQL Solution:\nSELECT \n  ad_id,\n  ROUND(\n    100.0 * COUNT(CASE WHEN event_type = 'tap' THEN 1 END) /\n    NULLIF(COUNT(CASE WHEN event_type = 'impression' THEN 1 END), 0),\n    2\n  ) AS tap_rate\nFROM ad_events\nGROUP BY ad_id;\n\nCommon Interview Trap:\nForgetting NULLIF to protect against division by zero when an ad has zero impressions, or using COUNT('tap') which counts all rows regardless of string value.\n\nKey Engineering Takeaway:\nCOUNT(CASE WHEN condition THEN 1 END) ignores NULLs when the condition is false, allowing clean single-pass pivot aggregations.\n\nDid you get it right? Share your thought process below.\nNIKHILs TECH Studio | India's Practice Gym for the AI Era",
