    "sql_solution": "SELECT \n  LOWER(TRIM(email)) AS clean_email,\n  COUNT(DISTINCT contact_id) AS accounts\nFROM contacts\nGROUP BY LOWER(TRIM(email))\nHAVING COUNT(DISTINCT contact_id) > 1\nORDER BY accounts DESC;",
    "common_mistake": "Grouping by raw email without applying normalization (LOWER and TRIM), which treats 'John@domain.com' and 'john@domain.com ' as different emails.",
