    "topic": "First-Touch Attribution for High-Value Members",
    "difficulty": "Advanced",
    "hook": "Enterprise accounts take 9 months to close. How do you trace a $100k contract back to the very first whitepaper they downloaded 270 days ago?",
    "scenario": "Tables:\n1. customer_touchpoints (touch_id, org_id, touch_type, touch_time)\n2. contracts (contract_id, org_id, contract_value, signed_at)\n\nYou need to find the touch_type of the earliest recorded touchpoint for each contract where contract_value >= 50000.",
    "question": "Which window query accurately surfaces the first-touch channel for each enterprise contract?",
    "option_a": "WITH ranked_touches AS (SELECT c.contract_id, t.touch_type, ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY c.contract_id ORDER BY t.touch_time ASC) as rn FROM contracts c JOIN customer_touchpoints t ON c.org_id = t.org_id AND t.touch_time <= c.signed_at WHERE c.contract_value >= 50000) SELECT contract_id, touch_type FROM ranked_touches WHERE rn = 1;",
    "option_b": "SELECT c.contract_id, MIN(t.touch_type) FROM contracts c JOIN customer_touchpoints t ON c.org_id = t.org_id GROUP BY c.contract_id;",
    "option_c": "SELECT contract_id, FIRST_VALUE(touch_type) OVER (ORDER BY contract_value DESC) FROM contracts JOIN customer_touchpoints USING (org_id);",
    "option_d": "SELECT org_id, touch_type FROM customer_touchpoints WHERE touch_time = '2026-01-01';",
    "correct_answer": "A",
    "post_content": "Day 21 of 30: Practical SQL & Business Analytics Challenges\nTopic: First-Touch Attribution for High-Value Members (Advanced)\n\nEnterprise accounts take 9 months to close. How do you trace a $100k contract back to the very first whitepaper they downloaded 270 days ago?\n\nThe Business Scenario:\nTables:\n1. customer_touchpoints (touch_id, org_id, touch_type, touch_time)\n2. contracts (contract_id, org_id, contract_value, signed_at)\n\nYou need to find the touch_type of the earliest recorded touchpoint for each contract where contract_value >= 50000.\n\nThe Challenge:\nWhich window query accurately surfaces the first-touch channel for each enterprise contract?\n\nA) WITH ranked_touches AS (SELECT c.contract_id, t.touch_type, ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY c.contract_id ORDER BY t.touch_time ASC) as rn FROM contracts c JOIN customer_touchpoints t ON c.org_id = t.org_id AND t.touch_time <= c.signed_at WHERE c.contract_value >= 50000) SELECT contract_id, touch_type FROM ranked_touches WHERE rn = 1;\nB) SELECT c.contract_id, MIN(t.touch_type) FROM contracts c JOIN customer_touchpoints t ON c.org_id = t.org_id GROUP BY c.contract_id;\nC) SELECT contract_id, FIRST_VALUE(touch_type) OVER (ORDER BY contract_value DESC) FROM contracts JOIN customer_touchpoints USING (org_id);\nD) SELECT org_id, touch_type FROM customer_touchpoints WHERE touch_time = '2026-01-01';\n\nDrop your answer (A, B, C, or D) in the comments along with your reasoning.\nTomorrow at 01:30 PM IST, we post the complete engineering breakdown and SQL solution in the comments.\n\nNIKHILs TECH Studio | India's Practice Gym for the AI Era\nLearn. Practice. Simulate. Grow.\n\n#SQL #DataAnalytics #DataEngineering #BusinessIntelligence #InterviewPrep #TechCareers #NTSCommand",
    "answer_comment": "Day 21 Solution Breakdown: First-Touch Attribution for High-Value Members\nCorrect Answer: Option A\n\nWhy this is the correct engineering approach:\nThe SQL Solution:\nWITH first_touch_ranked AS (\n  SELECT \n    c.contract_id,\n    c.contract_value,\n    t.touch_type,\n    t.touch_time,\n    ROW_NUMBER() OVER (\n      PARTITION BY c.contract_id \n      ORDER BY t.touch_time ASC\n    ) AS rn\n  FROM contracts c\n  INNER JOIN customer_touchpoints t \n    ON c.org_id = t.org_id \n   AND t.touch_time <= c.signed_at\n  WHERE c.contract_value >= 50000\n)\nSELECT contract_id, touch_type, touch_time\nFROM first_touch_ranked\nWHERE rn = 1;\n\nCommon Interview Trap:\nOption B uses MIN(touch_type), which sorts touch_type alphabetically (e.g., 'AdWords' beats 'Webinar') rather than chronologically.\n\nKey Engineering Takeaway:\nFirst-touch attribution requires chronological ordering (ORDER BY touch_time ASC) partitioned by contract or customer ID.\n\nDid you get it right? Share your thought process below.\nNIKHILs TECH Studio | India's Practice Gym for the AI Era",
    "hashtags": "#SQL #DataAnalytics #DataEngineering #BusinessIntelligence #InterviewPrep #TechCareers #NTSCommand",
